  "critique": {
    "axis": "accessibility",
    "evidence": "Keyboard traversal and visible focus passed for all expected controls at every viewport; no touch-target or section overflow violations were measured, and reduced-motion sampling found no element movement. However, contrast remains unverified for nine SVG chart labels at every viewport, including axis ticks and FPR labels. The charts’ accessible names are concatenated raw labels such as “100%0%25%50%75%100%,” with no screen-reader usability proof. Header contrast is also incomplete on tablet and mobile.",
    "fix": "Give each chart a concise accessible name and text/table equivalent, remove meaningless raw SVG focus behavior unless genuine keyboard interaction exists, and measure/fix WCAG contrast for every SVG label and responsive header link against its rendered background.",
